{{!
    @template local_catquizlab/statuscard

    One stateful thing, said the same way as every other: what it is, the
    evidence, and the one thing to do about it.

    A component with nothing to do about it has no action, and that is a
    statement rather than a gap — buttons on healthy things teach people to
    press buttons.

    Classes required for JS: none.
    Data attributes required for JS: none.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * level - good, watch or bad
    * good, watch, bad - flags for the level
    * state - what it is
    * reason - the evidence
    * action - label, url, command, and runid or classname, plus sesskey; or null

    Example context (json):
    {
        "level": "bad",
        "good": false,
        "watch": false,
        "bad": true,
        "state": "Waiting for a worker",
        "reason": "6 attempt(s) claimed by nobody",
        "action": {"label": "Start workers", "url": "/local/catquizlab/runs.php", "command": "provision", "runid": 4, "sesskey": "abc123"},
        "region": "catquizlab-queue"
    }
}}
<div class="d-flex align-items-start justify-content-between">
    <div>
        <span class="badge {{#good}}badge-success{{/good}}{{#watch}}badge-warning{{/watch}}{{#bad}}badge-danger{{/bad}}">
            {{#good}}&check;{{/good}}{{#watch}}!{{/watch}}{{#bad}}&times;{{/bad}}
        </span>
        <strong{{#region}} data-region="{{.}}-state"{{/region}}>{{state}}</strong>
        <div class="small text-muted"{{#region}} data-region="{{.}}-reason"{{/region}}>{{reason}}</div>
    </div>
    {{#action}}
        {{!
            Posted, not linked. A state change behind a GET is one a prefetcher,
            a crawler or a back button can make on somebody's behalf.
        }}
        {{#command}}
            <form method="post" action="{{url}}" class="d-inline ml-2 flex-shrink-0">
                <input type="hidden" name="sesskey" value="{{sesskey}}">
                <input type="hidden" name="action" value="{{command}}">
                {{#runid}}<input type="hidden" name="runid" value="{{.}}">{{/runid}}
                {{#classname}}<input type="hidden" name="classname" value="{{.}}">{{/classname}}
                <button type="submit" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary">{{label}}</button>
            </form>
        {{/command}}
        {{!
            An action that only takes somebody to another page is a link. A form
            for it would post nothing and mean nothing.
        }}
        {{^command}}
            <a href="{{url}}" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary ml-2 flex-shrink-0">{{label}}</a>
        {{/command}}
    {{/action}}
</div>
